  <main_text>
    <l n="1">Idque probatur de jure cano-</l>
    <l n="2">nico, quicquid in contrarium</l>
    <l n="3">statuant multi canoniftæ. Ne-</l>
    <l n="4">que enim eo jure, ullam incur-</l>
    <l n="5">rit irregularitatem, qui mor-</l>
    <l n="6">tem aliter evitare non valens,</l>
    <l n="7">suum mutilat, vel occidit in-</l>
    <l n="8">vaforem. Cumque canon non</l>
    <l n="9">diftinguat, inter mutilantem</l>
    <l n="10">vel occidentem armis æquali-</l>
    <l n="11">bus aut inæqualibus, modo</l>
    <l n="12">subfit periculum.Et illud sub-</l>
    <l n="13">esse possit, licet inæqualibus</l>
    <l n="14">armis, quis petatur; frustra jure</l>
    <l n="15">non limitante, limitationem</l>
    <l n="16">talem adhibemus.</l>
    <l n="17" para="true">Neque hic leges diffenti-</l>
    <l n="18">unt, quæ indiftinctè, propul-</l>
    <l n="19">sionem periculi imminentis</l>
    <l n="20">admittunt. Cum quisque id</l>
    <l n="21">jure fecisse dicatur, quali quali</l>
    <l n="22">id fecerit instrumento, quod</l>
    <l n="23">ad corporis sui fecerit tutelam.</l>
    <l n="24" para="true">Accedit, quod cuique liceat</l>
    <l n="25">telo aggredientem interimere.</l>
    <l n="26">Verùm <i>teli</i> nomine etiam in-</l>
  </main_text>
